      'en': 'Answer: <b>から</b>. Here rice is <b>the raw material</b>; after processing you can no longer see its original form, so から is used.<br>Distractor: <b>によって</b> marks <b>the party who does the action, or the cause of an event</b> (外国人によって 作られた / 地震によって こわされた). Rice here is <b>the material being processed</b>, not the one acting, so it takes から. This question is deliberately paired with the previous one to make you tell these apart.<br>By the way, for a material whose <b>original form is still visible after processing</b> (木で 作った いす), <b>で</b> is the usual choice.<br>Summary: <b>a person → によって</b>, <b>raw material (transformed) → から</b>, <b>material (still visible) → で</b>.',
